WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.808
Telo Ride now installs from Chrome or Edge, and opens in its own window, one tap

00:00:07.808 --> 00:00:09.023
from the bike.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.572
A web app manifest names it Telo Ride, and opens it at the start, standalone, in the

00:00:15.572 --> 00:00:17.122
dark ink of the app.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.573
Its icons are the logo mark on ink: one hundred and ninety-two and five hundred and

00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:32.415
twelve pixels, and a maskable one inside the safe zone.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.146
The spec asks Chromium itself for the manifest it read, and its reasons not to

00:00:41.146 --> 00:00:45.817
install. There are none. The service worker keeps the icons offline.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.013
Home, where the installed app opens, from a phone to the full screen.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:03.965
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:08.821
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:08.821 --> 00:01:10.492
every hill and interval.

00:01:10.838 --> 00:01:16.016
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:16.016 --> 00:01:21.464
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:21.464 --> 00:01:24.454
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:27.291
A custom workout lives under Profile.
